{% extends "products/postgresql/base.njk" %}
{% set platformBaseTemplate = "rhel-10-or-ol-10" %}
{% block prerequisites %}
{{ super() }}
- Enable additional repositories to resolve dependencies:
  ```shell
  ARCH=$( /bin/arch ) subscription-manager repos --enable "codeready-builder-for-rhel-10-${ARCH}-rpms"
  ```
- Make sure DNF installs PostgreSQL from the EDB repository.

  On RHEL 10.2, DNF can select PostgreSQL packages from the AppStream repository instead of the EDB repository. To make DNF prefer the EDB repository, set the EDB repository priority to 1.

  To make the change permanent, enter:

  ```shell
  sudo dnf config-manager --setopt=enterprisedb-enterprise.priority=1 --save enterprisedb-enterprise
  ```

  Alternatively, to apply the priority to a single installation only, add the `--setopt` option to the install command:

  ```shell
  sudo dnf install --setopt=enterprisedb-enterprise.priority=1 postgresql<xx>-server postgresql<xx>-contrib
  ```

  Where `<xx>` is the version of PostgreSQL you're installing.
{% endblock prerequisites %}
